<v David Zax>That's my producer saying, why don't you tell us and we'll determine if we can play it.
<v David Zax>那是我的制作人在说，为什么你不告诉我们，我们会决定是否能播放。

00:30:20.920 --> 00:30:30.070
<v Jack Bailey>I said, you god damn mother fucking son of a bitch, you didn't read your goddamn file until this weekend, did you?
<v Jack Bailey>我说，你这个该死的他妈的混蛋，你直到这个周末才读你的档案，对吧？

00:30:30.070 --> 00:30:47.240
<v David Zax>In other words, you just realized how weak your case was. If you'd done that months ago you would have saved me and my client a lot of trouble. Scott Brady declined to comment for our story, but a colleague claims that he was ready for trial that day.
<v David Zax>换句话说，你刚意识到你的案子有多薄弱。如果你几个月前这样做，你就会省去我和我客户很多麻烦。Scott Brady拒绝就我们的报道发表评论，但一位同事声称他那天已经准备好进行审判了。

00:30:47.240 --> 00:31:05.740
<v Jack Bailey>So Jack has this side conversation with the DA and knows the charges against Trastavien are going to be dropped. But nobody else does. Not the judge, not Tammy and Trastavien, who are there after all these months of preparation waiting for the trial to start. The gavel strikes. The court's in session.
<v Jack Bailey>所以Jack和地区检察官进行了这次侧谈，知道针对Trastavien的指控要被撤销。但其他人不知道。不是法官，不是Tammy和Trastavien，他们在经过这几个月的准备后都在那里等待审判开始。法槌敲响。法庭开庭了。

00:31:05.740 --> 00:31:24.980
<v Tammy Burdine>We are first. The assistant DA gets up and says your honor, in the matter State vs. Trastavien Hardy, and then he says, your honor, the state is dismissing the charges with nothing else. And that was it.
<v Tammy Burdine>我们是第一个。助理地方检察官站起来说，法官阁下，在State vs. Trastavien Hardy一案中，然后他说，法官阁下，政府撤销指控，没有别的了。就这样。

00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:39.870
<v Trastavien Hardy>As soon as I walked up there I'm like, oh yes. Thank you, Jesus. That was the first thing I said, really. I was like thank you, Jesus. I really felt overwhelmed. I was like about time.
<v Trastavien Hardy>当我走上去时，我心想，噢耶。感谢耶稣。那是第一件我说的话，真的。我当时想感谢耶稣。我真的感到不知所措。我当时想终于到了。

00:31:39.870 --> 00:32:07.120
<v Tammy Burdine>But I'm all of a sudden going what? What just happened? We're here. We're ready. They just stomped the show. The show, is just-- but that's what I wanted. But then I won't know the outcome. But this is the outcome. But wait a minute, they need to know that Mr Hardy didn't do this.
<v Tammy Burdine>但我突然在想什么？刚刚发生了什么？我们在这里。我们准备好了。他们就这样结束了演出。演出，就是——但这正是我想的。但我不会知道结果。但这就是结果。但等等，他们需要知道Hardy先生没做这件事。

00:32:07.120 --> 00:32:11.530
<v Tammy Burdine>And then Mr Bailey, he said, your honor--
<v Tammy Burdine>然后Bailey先生，他说，法官阁下——

